<feed xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom"><title>France 24 - International breaking news, top stories and headlines</title><subtitle type="html">Breaking news and world news from France 24 on Business, Sports, Culture. Video news. News from the US, Europe, Asia Pacific, Africa, Middle East, America</subtitle><id>https://www.france24.com/en/rss</id><updated>2026-09-14T15:07:46Z</updated><author><name>rssync</name></author><link rel="self" href="rss" type="application/atom+xml" /><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/rss" type="application/rss+xml" /><entry><title>Countries turn to coal to avoid shipping disruptions in the Strait of Hormuz</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:65a2e5fb12c894ecb110c083bf724f49bffe67e70364773895c673d351291a7f</id><updated>2026-09-14T15:06:37Z</updated><published>2026-09-14T14:08:22Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/down-to-earth/20260914-countries-turn-to-coal-to-avoid-shipping-disruptions-in-the-strait-of-hormuz--68a150198937.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/down-to-earth/20260914-countries-turn-to-coal-to-avoid-shipping-disruptions-in-the-strait-of-hormuz" /><summary type="html">The US-Israel war on Iran has shaken global energy markets and coal is no exception. Countries around the world are turning to the highly polluting source of power in a bid to avoid shipping disruptions in the Strait of Hormuz. According to the International Energy Agency, global coal demand is forecast to rise by ​1.2% this year to a record 8.94 billion ‌tonnes. FRANCE 24’s Environment Editor Valerie Dekimpe has the details in this edition.</summary><category term="Down to Earth" /></entry><entry><title>Keziah Jones goes symphonic</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:c2c16431c13fbf50cc858b1c4055f8d79af8b510428d6ce95e23f26f658dc1b8</id><updated>2026-09-14T15:06:39Z</updated><published>2026-09-14T13:55:25Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/arts24/20260914-keziah-jones-goes-symphonic--0f4900128715.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/arts24/20260914-keziah-jones-goes-symphonic" /><summary type="html">This week arts24 talks to Nigerian Blues Funk Artist Keziah Jones ahead of his Symphonic premier at la Scène Musicale on September 29 as part of Jazz &amp; Musique du Monde season. He tells FRANCE 24's Marjorie Hache about his music and about working with arranger Pierre Bertrand. Plus, we take a look at new releases by Beck, Miley Cyrus and Beabadobee.</summary><category term="arts24" /></entry><entry><title>How will EU respond to Russian attack on train near Polish border?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:1dae823602003e7dd68b656b05843db11116bccc1b24ffaef0e66892cc9e1ad8</id><updated>2026-09-14T15:06:42Z</updated><published>2026-09-14T13:42:14Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20260914-how-will-eu-respond-to-russian-attack-on-train-near-polish-border--acf1d7e6d739.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20260914-how-will-eu-respond-to-russian-attack-on-train-near-polish-border" /><summary type="html">The EU's top diplomat said Monday that Russian strikes which hit a Warsaw-bound train near Ukraine's border with Poland shortly after top Western figures passed through were meant to "scare" off Kyiv's backers. "It is clearly meant to scare Western countries from supporting Ukraine, from going to Ukraine to show support," foreign policy chief Kaja Kallas said, urging Kyiv's backers to do "the opposite". France 24's Dave Keating reports from Brussels.</summary></entry><entry><title>'What makes China work despite the pain in society?' asks analyst Dan Wang</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:f0561276898a2b58e7b03f9f68a05d8cce71fad1e0a75de1f3a53410dbf85d9c</id><updated>2026-09-14T15:06:45Z</updated><published>2026-09-14T13:30:45Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/what-makes-china-work-despite-the-pain-in-society-asks-analyst-dan-wang--d40c2ced80a4.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/what-makes-china-work-despite-the-pain-in-society-asks-analyst-dan-wang" /><summary type="html">In this edition of Perspective, FRANCE 24’s Stuart Norval speaks to Dan Wang, a China expert whose book ‘Breakneck:  China’s Quest to Engineer the Future’ is a New York Times bestseller. It takes a close look at Chinese life and draws from Wang’s own ten years of living there. Wang says the China and the US are some of the most similar people in the world, as they are both hustlers and take shortcuts.</summary><category term="Perspective" /></entry><entry><title>French 2027 presidential elections: Why Gen Z has mobilised for Mélenchon</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:37f43a85161b94f711f7e97a8602736a58f8bc8d578d470b425979987c6be1a7</id><updated>2026-09-14T15:06:48Z</updated><published>2026-09-14T13:05:26Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20260914-french-2027-presidential-elections-why-gen-z-has-mobilised-for-m_lenchon--b3d1ffef001b.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20260914-french-2027-presidential-elections-why-gen-z-has-mobilised-for-m%C3%A9lenchon" /><summary type="html">🇫🇷 French far-left presidential candidate Jean-Luc #Mélenchon is both highly controversial and a #GenZ favourite.
 
Mélenchon's young supporters express admiration for his promises to stage a "citizen's revolution",  redistrubute wealth, fight #climatechange and support #Palestine. The candidate's critics have accused him of complancency towards #Russia and antisemitism. 
 
Despite being divisive, recent polls predict that Mélenchon will qualify for the second round of #France's 2027 presidential #election, where he would likely face far-right candidate Marine #LePen.
 
So, why has France's Gen Z mobilised for Mélenchon?
 
🔴 FRANCE 24's Gabrielle Nadler spoke to young voters to find out.</summary></entry><entry><title>Should the brakes be put on AI?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:94b7acb6ad482347e8b9801c1547f9f277b45a7ed049b06a48ac59ffa4c87fce</id><updated>2026-09-14T15:06:51Z</updated><published>2026-09-14T13:02:57Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20260914-should-the-brakes-be-put-on-ai--df0737934395.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20260914-should-the-brakes-be-put-on-ai" /><summary type="html">US President Donald Trump says he is worried about America giving China an edge in the Artificial Intelligence market if too many rules and regulations are put on it. In recent days industry insiders, including top executives at Open AI and Anthropic, have once again sounded the alarm, saying that the way AI is being developed could threaten humanity and calling for more checks to be put in place.</summary></entry><entry><title>Trump criticises 'negative forces' seeking to slow AI development</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:50d82d9346e51b34f803ba75b3a636b933af5770e7913b632ec00e403111ee0c</id><updated>2026-09-14T15:06:54Z</updated><published>2026-09-14T12:49:02Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20260914-trump-criticises-negative-forces-seeking-to-slow-ai-development--bd4a498a26cf.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20260914-trump-criticises-negative-forces-seeking-to-slow-ai-development" /><summary type="html">US President Donald Trump on Sunday slammed critics of artificial intelligence (AI) who warned firms to slow down development, branding them "negative" forces. The comments came soon after OpenAI CEO Sam Altman announced his company will not go public this year, citing safety concerns.</summary></entry><entry><title>Climate catastrophe leaves Nepal mourning while the search for the missing continues</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:28c1f052e1fce79e6e129529164d688cab47a2e6411d2f21331f6f1af9eaa49d</id><updated>2026-09-14T15:06:57Z</updated><published>2026-09-14T12:43:12Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/focus/20260914-climate-catastrophe-leaves-nepal-mourning-while-the-search-for-the-missing-continues--40d634ca2dd0.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/focus/20260914-climate-catastrophe-leaves-nepal-mourning-while-the-search-for-the-missing-continues" /><summary type="html">The himalayan flash flood that devastated northern Nepal on August 26 was an unprecedented disaster. The death toll continues to rise, with nearly 1,400 people now confirmed dead and 5,130 still missing, including around 600 foreign nationals from 35 countries.</summary><category term="Focus" /></entry><entry><title>Was Russian train strike meant to 'scare' the West?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:92669076813aefdcf84b8a30776121ad294a606b8d8264f215d0ddd3506bcae8</id><updated>2026-09-14T15:07:00Z</updated><published>2026-09-14T11:41:49Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20260914-was-russian-train-strike-meant-to-scare-the-west--eb42a4961f45.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20260914-was-russian-train-strike-meant-to-scare-the-west" /><summary type="html">The EU's top diplomat said Monday that Russian strikes which hit a Warsaw-bound train near Ukraine's border with Poland shortly after top Western figures passed through were meant to "scare" off Kyiv's backers. France 24's correspondent in Kyiv, Gulliver Cragg, has the latest.</summary></entry><entry><title>Russia strikes Ukraine with drones as Poland warns of 'escalation'</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:fd1ef454cfecb8775979c6bd1d458f17281be8ffc157c297cff6d704d9d41b62</id><updated>2026-09-14T15:07:03Z</updated><published>2026-09-14T11:37:33Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20260914-russia-strikes-ukraine-with-drones-as-poland-warns-of-escalation--d24f4d1e5f89.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20260914-russia-strikes-ukraine-with-drones-as-poland-warns-of-escalation" /><summary type="html">Russia continues its ramped-up air campaign against Ukraine, launching 453 drones in an overnight blitz. One drone struck 800 metres from a border crossing with Poland prompting the polish military to scramble fighter jets and helicopters.</summary></entry><entry><title>Thousands rally in support of Brazil's Lula as election campaigning heats up</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:6883d5d5c35081ef9153b1af4d9b996c9368a6f6a4a56e5567617101d08354f9</id><updated>2026-09-14T15:07:06Z</updated><published>2026-09-14T10:59:53Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20260914-thousands-rally-in-support-of-brazil-s-lula-as-election-campaigning-heats-up--a8fa79947199.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20260914-thousands-rally-in-support-of-brazil-s-lula-as-election-campaigning-heats-up" /><summary type="html">With Brazil set to hold a Presidential election on October 4th, supporters of both incumbent Luiz Inacio Lula Da Silva and his main opponent Flavio Bolsonaro have been taking to the streets. Polls have the candidates, who are on opposite ends of political spectrum, neck and neck.</summary></entry><entry><title>Dozens arrested as Turkish police raid LGBTQ bars, activists' homes</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:f96370d9079a8ccb5d4efc570cdb43af71abbcad129f4450117a789c06b95cee</id><updated>2026-09-14T15:07:09Z</updated><published>2026-09-14T10:58:30Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20260914-dozens-arrested-as-turkish-police-raid-lgbtq-bars-activists-homes--19f8c8b9504f.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20260914-dozens-arrested-as-turkish-police-raid-lgbtq-bars-activists-homes" /><summary type="html">Turkish police on Sunday made dozens of arrests in a slew of raids on gay bars and the homes of LGBTQ activists. Authorities said the raids came in the context of the "Decade of the Family" proclaimed by Turkish President Recep Tayyip Erdogan, aimed at "protecting our children, the institution of the family and social order".</summary></entry><entry><title>A 'complicated autumn' awaits Sweden after knife-edge vote</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:fe30dc3a2ded0e2f0d71c526182565e2996a4b905482c9b8d505ca3abe3a04e0</id><updated>2026-09-14T15:07:12Z</updated><published>2026-09-14T10:56:35Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20260914-a-complicated-autumn-awaits-sweden-after-knife-edge-vote--b980c5153729.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20260914-a-complicated-autumn-awaits-sweden-after-knife-edge-vote" /><summary type="html">Sweden's general election remained too close to call early Monday, with nearly 90 percent of votes counted. Four opposition parties led by Social Democrat Magdalena Andersson held a one-seat parliamentary lead over Prime Minister Ulf Kristersson's right-wing bloc, which includes the Sweden Democrats, as both leaders said they were ready to govern.</summary></entry><entry><title>‘They drove us from our land’: Thousands displaced by Yemen conflict</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:2cd05c423b0a3456e2e7f26cce057d776c7a654750a98757348f81ff90935aea</id><updated>2026-09-14T15:07:15Z</updated><published>2026-09-14T10:22:45Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20260914-they-drove-us-from-our-land-thousands-displaced-by-yemen-conflict--560bed71a167.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20260914-they-drove-us-from-our-land-thousands-displaced-by-yemen-conflict" /><summary type="html">According to the UN, more than 86,000 people have been displaced in Yemen since July, following fighting between the Iran-backed Houthis rebels and government forces. Many have fled to refugee camps in government-controlled Aden, while others have headed to neighbouring Djibouti.</summary></entry><entry><title>Yemen govt forces hit back as conflict with Houthis intensifies</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:0d0b978e14328de79ff9613f862be1e2d45608e565858542457d3214817eb577</id><updated>2026-09-14T15:07:18Z</updated><published>2026-09-14T10:16:14Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20260914-yemen-govt-forces-hit-back-as-conflict-with-houthis-intensifies--ad9a5b2117f1.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20260914-yemen-govt-forces-hit-back-as-conflict-with-houthis-intensifies" /><summary type="html">The conflict in Yemen intensified on Sunday, as government forces launched attacks against Iran-backed Houthi rebels along the Red Sea and Houthis fired into neighboring Saudi Arabia, which supports Yemen’s government. The Yemeni government vowed to send more forces to the Red Sea coast and one official conceded a “painful” defeat last week when Houthis captured the port city of Mokha and an island on the Bab el-Mandeb Strait, a crucial shipping alternative to the Strait of Hormuz.</summary></entry><entry><title>'Palpable tension' as Philippines Muslim region holds first elections</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:59168346493162b12ec483c809eee0cbba6eb4f88383ea1624eb83796b4f6115</id><updated>2026-09-14T15:07:21Z</updated><published>2026-09-14T10:10:14Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20260914-palpable-tension-as-philippines-muslim-region-holds-first-elections--6247937eb01b.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20260914-palpable-tension-as-philippines-muslim-region-holds-first-elections" /><summary type="html">A predominantly Muslim region in the southern Philippines held its first parliamentary elections on Monday, seen as a crucial step in the long quest for self-rule after decades of insurgency and violence. Reporting from the region, France 24’s look Jan Camenzind Broomby, takes a look at the vote’s significance, as well as the tensions surrounding election day.</summary></entry><entry><title>Retrial over 2018 France terror attack begins</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:38698cea50bdea893e74ffc6439ca0c74652636037d2c83ac020d81f5223df0a</id><updated>2026-09-14T15:07:24Z</updated><published>2026-09-14T10:02:28Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20260914-retrial-over-2018-france-terror-attack-begins--9af0b753577d.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20260914-retrial-over-2018-france-terror-attack-begins" /><summary type="html">The retrial of three defendants linked to a 2018 terror attack in a supermarket in southern France that left four people dead begins in Paris on Monday. The defendants include the former partner of the attacker himself, who was shot dead by the authorities. France 24’s Luke Shrago has more.</summary></entry><entry><title>Can Sweden restore welfare system amid increased defense spending?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:8b87c971d5489491e0b9c0f7474699c396ffbd9e618cc5fbeffe1e42edfc146e</id><updated>2026-09-14T15:07:27Z</updated><published>2026-09-14T09:25:25Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20260914-can-sweden-restore-welfare-system-amid-increased-defense-spending--2284d9295923.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20260914-can-sweden-restore-welfare-system-amid-increased-defense-spending" /><summary type="html">While the results of Sweden's general election remain too close to call, it looks as though the country's center-left opposition may get the chance to form a new government after four years under a right-wing coalition. The runup to the vote was dominated domestic economic issues, including the future of the country's once famously generous welfare state. But Sweden's international financial commitments - notably to increased defense spending following its decision to join NATO amid Russia's war on Ukraine - are likely to limit its options.</summary></entry><entry><title>Sweden faces political uncertainty after knife-edge election</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:a64b807a6e798d53519dc02a18247b6eed13a4fe47379c1ec798832c2f6e455e</id><updated>2026-09-14T15:07:30Z</updated><published>2026-09-14T09:25:14Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/europe/20260914-sweden-faces-political-uncertainty-after-knife-edge-election--1048b951361e.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20260914-sweden-faces-political-uncertainty-after-knife-edge-election" /><summary type="html">Sweden was bracing for a protracted struggle to form a government on Monday after election results showed a thin and uncertain lead for the left-wing opposition, while the far-right Sweden Democrats lost ground for the first time since entering parliament 16 years ago.</summary><category term="Europe" /></entry><entry><title>Centre-left holds narrow lead in knife-edge Sweden vote</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:159573f8d4414184f8cf1d98936ebe7e566cbaf9fa3c823ec17373685fc57c41</id><updated>2026-09-14T15:07:33Z</updated><published>2026-09-14T09:20:50Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20260914-centre-left-holds-narrow-lead-in-knife-edge-sweden-vote--6b929ca411bd.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20260914-centre-left-holds-narrow-lead-in-knife-edge-sweden-vote" /><summary type="html">Sweden's centre-left opposition on ​Monday looked the most likely to form the next government as preliminary election results showed it holding a narrow three-seat lead over the right-wing ruling parties with most of the votes counted after Sunday's vote. Party leaders, however, have been cautious about claiming victory or accepting defeat with 353 election districts still to be counted ‌and overseas votes not likely to be tallied until Wednesday.</summary></entry><entry><title>As Yemen conflict intensifies, Iran the winner?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:72d415486f7abb534cc4369d56bc0a7b3f732b21e55ac5aa4da95d5b6a94db93</id><updated>2026-09-14T15:07:36Z</updated><published>2026-09-14T09:16:07Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20260914-as-yemen-conflict-intensifies-iran-the-winner--014827183700.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20260914-as-yemen-conflict-intensifies-iran-the-winner" /><summary type="html">The conflict in Yemen intensified on Sunday, as government forces launched attacks against Iran-backed Houthi rebels along the Red Sea and Houthis fired into neighboring Saudi Arabia, which supports Yemen’s government. It comes after Houthis captured the port city of Mokha and an island on the Bab el-Mandeb Strait, a crucial shipping alternative to the Strait of Hormuz. The adds pressure on global oil supplies and prices, and that could give Iran leverage in its war with the United States. Andrew Hilliar has more.</summary></entry><entry><title>Indonesia: Rescuers resume search for 129 missing after ferry capsized</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:ac0cf75ec8ed3ac54637c403bc18988e45d03a299321d219ca366c159429de2e</id><updated>2026-09-14T15:07:39Z</updated><published>2026-09-14T08:57:56Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20260914-indonesia-rescuers-resume-search-for-129-missing-after-ferry-capsized--3f97e7973f03.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20260914-indonesia-rescuers-resume-search-for-129-missing-after-ferry-capsized" /><summary type="html">Hundreds of Indonesian rescuers including the coast guard and the navy raced on Monday to board a passenger ship that capsized in the Java Sea over the weekend as they searched for 129 people still missing, officials said, with the confirmed death toll at six.</summary></entry><entry><title>'State-led discrimination': Turkey detains dozens after raids targeting LGBTQ groups</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:6e07fb0c8afe837a1d6c1c40f5a11cbaf6463d58e3ea4af51caf48c2bca78800</id><updated>2026-09-14T15:07:42Z</updated><published>2026-09-14T08:45:53Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20260914-state-led-discrimination-turkey-detains-dozens-after-raids-targeting-lgbtq-groups--620eaaff9e07.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20260914-state-led-discrimination-turkey-detains-dozens-after-raids-targeting-lgbtq-groups" /><summary type="html">Turkish police on Sunday arrested at least 60 people in mass raids on gay bars and the homes of LGBTQ activists, in what authorities said was an operation aimed at boosting traditional family values. The raids sparked condemnation from rights groups and opposition parties, as well as the European Union parliament's rapporteur on Turkey. France 24’s Jasper Mortimer has the latest.</summary></entry><entry><title>Who is Iran's 'influential spymaster' Hossein Taeb and does he pull the strings?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:a8e167100e4db33159dfe1aa1b00cf27653716cbdc0ceeeca1b9b7ffe6cbeffa</id><updated>2026-09-14T15:07:46Z</updated><published>2026-09-14T08:40:24Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/press-review/20260914-who-is-iran-s-influential-spymaster-hossein-taeb-and-does-he-pull-the-strings--1568e0ad59bc.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/press-review/20260914-who-is-iran-s-influential-spymaster-hossein-taeb-and-does-he-pull-the-strings" /><summary type="html">PRESS REVIEW – Monday, September 14: The New York Times released an exclusive report titled “How Iran’s hard-liners prevailed and sabotaged the US peace deal”. Also: Trump says AI fears are "exaggerated", but reports show a different reality.</summary><category term="Press Review" /></entry></feed>
